  "description": "FOSZIZ crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H105 Dy4 N16 O25 3+,2(C2 H3 N1),3(N1 O3 1-),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.551-5.084 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.59-179.20°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(μ4-OH){(R)-HL2}8](NO3)3·2CH3CN·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
